-- title:
--   Diamond automorphisms fix functions of level Γ₀(N)
-- statement:
--   Fix $N \geq 1$, a subgroup $H \leq (\mathbb{Z}/N)^\times$ and a unit $c \in (\mathbb{Z}/N)^\times$. Let $x$ be an element of `xHFunctionFieldBar N H`, the intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ generated by the coefficientwise images, under the map `coeffEmb` induced by $\mathbb{Q} \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, of the elements of the rational function field `xHFunctionFieldC ℚ N H` $\subseteq \mathbb{Q}((q))$. Let $y \in \mathbb{Q}((q))$ lie in `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ (Gamma0 N)`, the subfield of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the quotients $\mathrm{intSeriesC}_{\mathbb{Q}}(p_f)/\mathrm{intSeriesC}_{\mathbb{Q}}(p_g)$ attached to pairs of modular forms $f, g$ of some weight $k$ for $\Gamma_0(N)$ (viewed inside $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{R})$) having integral $q$-expansions $p_f, p_g \in \mathbb{Z}[[q]]$ with $\mathrm{intSeriesC}_{\mathbb{Q}}(p_g) \neq 0$. Assume the Laurent series underlying $x$ is the coefficientwise image of $y$. Then $x$ is fixed by `diamondAutHBar N H c`, the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-algebra automorphism of `xHFunctionFieldBar N H` chosen to satisfy `IsDiamondAutHBar N H c` — that is, to send each $\mathrm{coeffEmb}(\mathrm{intSeriesC}_{\mathbb{Q}}(p_f)/\mathrm{intSeriesC}_{\mathbb{Q}}(p_g))$, for $f, g$ of level $\Gamma_H(N)$, to the image of the rational function whose $q$-expansion over $\mathbb{C}$ is that of $(f \mid_k \gamma)/(g \mid_k \gamma)$ for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(N)$ with upper-left entry congruent to $c$ — and taken to be the identity should no such automorphism exist.
--
--   This is the classical fact that the diamond operators $\langle c \rangle$ act trivially on the function field of $X_0(N)$, here in the geometric ($\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-rational) model of $X_H(N)$: any function on $X_H(N)$ whose $q$-expansion comes from level $\Gamma_0(N)$, such as $j(q)$ or $j(q^d)$ for $d \mid N$, is invariant. It is used in the construction of charts and units on $X_H(N)$ and in the identification of the Atkin–Lehner pull-backs, where the defining relations must be read modulo the diamond action.
-- source:
